Package: taxonAlign
Title: Align and Update Taxonomic Names Against Any Taxonomic Reference
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person(given = "Elizabeth", family = "Wenk", role = c("aut", "ctb", "cph"), email = "e.wenk@unsw.edu.au", comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-5640-5910")),
    person(given = "Fonti", family = "Kar", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "f.kar@unsw.edu.au", comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-2760-3974"))
    )
Description: Matches lists of raw taxon names, including misspelt, informal and
  morphospecies names, to a taxonomic reference, and updates them to their currently accepted
  names. The reference can be one or more released datasets (versioned, so results are
  reproducible) or the user's own tables, in a documented format, at any combination of
  taxonomic ranks. The companion package taxonAlign.dataprep builds and releases those
  datasets, and helps users turn their own references into the format.
